{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2221","published":"2026-05-09T11:11:12Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:51.829626353Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-33845"],"summary":"gnutls security update","details":"GnuTLS is a secure communications library implementing the SSL, TLS and DTLS protocols and technologies around them. It provides a simple C language application programming interface (API) to access the secure communications protocols as well as APIs to parse and write X.509, PKCS #12, and other required structures. The project strives to provide a secure communications back-end, simple to use and integrated with the rest of the base Linux libraries. A back-end designed to work and be secure out of the box, keeping the complexity of TLS and PKI out of application code.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw in GnuTLS DTLS handshake parsing allows malformed fragments with zero length and non-zero offset, leading to an integer underflow during reassembly and resulting in an out-of-bounds read. This issue is remotely exploitable and may cause information disclosure or denial of service.(CVE-2026-33845)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"gnutls","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/gnutls&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["gnutls-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","gnutls-dane-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","gnutls-debuginfo-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","gnutls-debugsource-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","gnutls-devel-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","gnutls-utils-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["gnutls-help-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.noarch.rpm"],"src":["gnutls-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["gnutls-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","gnutls-dane-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","gnutls-debuginfo-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","gnutls-debugsource-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","gnutls-devel-3.8.2-12.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm",